t task-native ledger heading\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"ledger_source_breadth\",\"description\":\"14 distinct cited sources\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"power_duration_reversal\",\"description\":\"no unnegated prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"pressure_unit_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"probability_measure_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"self_authorized_readiness\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"threshold_reversal\",\"description\":\"no prohibited relation conversion\",\"status\":\"pass\"}],\"evaluated_candidate_sha256\":\"82d14bff607d8e323899d09b72739ee4bf14bc067013c6675365b580093ecf5a\",\"evaluator_id\":\"solace-water-evaluator-v1\",\"passed\":false,\"raw_result_handle\":\"raw-tool://RESULT-016/evaluator\",\"raw_result_preserved_exactly\":true,\"returncode_class\":\"zero\",\"schema\":\"stable-candidate-bound-check-projection-v1\",\"volatile_fields_excluded\":true}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"delivery_ordinal\":18,\"exact_result_sha256\":\"972c0c4d8ddfdfc2ec2240151d07b3152636b8752921d96ae38f4d00f249dc00\",\"exact_result_size_bytes\":8434,\"object_id\":\"batch:BASTION:1-64+CIPHER:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"7a7e4e117076d9f65dc05bb16e1f9557f7de5652de35ef4eef509bc13ffd6631\",\"observed_ranges\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1}],\"previously_model_visible\":true,\"reopen_action\":{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-017\"},\"reopen_handle\":\"result://sha256/972c0c4d8ddfdfc2ec2240151d07b3152636b8752921d96ae38f4d00f249dc00\",\"resident\":false,\"result_id\":\"RESULT-017\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema_version\":\"ceiba-exact-result-receipt-v1\",\"source_id\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"BASTION\",\"CIPHER\"],\"source_path\":null,\"source_sha256\":null,\"source_size_bytes\":null,\"total_source_bytes\":7931}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"delivery_ordinal\":19,\"exact_result_sha256\":\"35ff36c72b28abded06ccd4c683cfc5f00550e4f488eba4fe65ef5b991500202\",\"exact_result_size_bytes\":8670,\"object_id\":\"batch:DELTA:1-64+INDIGO:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"c31f85d7dad24e54b12f4b0d24aacfd84098f9663ffb3d67510890c8cf67dda3\",\"observed_ranges\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"INDIGO\",\"start_line\":1}],\"previously_model_visible\":true,\"reopen_action\":{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-018\"},\"reopen_handle\":\"result://sha256/35ff36c72b28abded06ccd4c683cfc5f00550e4f488eba4fe65ef5b991500202\",\"resident\":false,\"result_id\":\"RESULT-018\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema_version\":\"ceiba-exact-result-receipt-v1\",\"source_id\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"DELTA\",\"INDIGO\"],\"source_path\":null,\"source_sha256\":null,\"source_size_bytes\":null,\"total_source_bytes\":8171}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"patch_decision\",\"edits\":[{\"new\":\"The north-zone distribution system currently holds a minimum pressure of 42 psi [BASTION]. The restoration gate requires at least 35 psi at every critical node for three consecutive thirty-minute windows; the current 42 psi reading does not by itself satisfy this multi-window requirement, and psi values must not be converted to kPa or treated as proof of water quality [BASTION]. Ridge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons; these are distinct measures and must not be conflated as treated reserve [BASTION]. DELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power; cavitation constraints limit shared-main capacity under staged demand conditions [DELTA, BASTION, ECHO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states: a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Residence time in the distribution loop must be verified against candidate-bound hydraulic model H12; any change to valve map V8 or controller firmware C11 invalidates prior residence-time evidence [MOSAIC]. The current minimum pressure of 42 psi exceeds the 30 psi isolation trigger but remains within the operational band defined by H12; no isolation action is currently indicated, though the three-consecutive-window restoration gate must still be met before hydraulic clearance can be claimed [BASTION, INDIGO].\",\"old\":\"The north-zone distribution system currently holds a minimum pressure of 42 psi [BASTION]. Ridge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons; these are distinct measures and must not be conflated as treated reserve [BASTION]. DELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power; cavitation constraints limit shared-main capacity under staged demand conditions [DELTA, BASTION, ECHO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states: a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Residence time in the distribution loop must be verified against candidate-bound hydraulic model H12; any change to valve map V8 or controller firmware C11 invalidates prior residence-time evidence [MOSAIC]. The current minimum pressure of 42 psi exceeds the 30 psi isolation trigger but remains within the operational band defined by H12; no isolation action is currently indicated [BASTION, INDIGO].\"},{\"new\":\"Clearance requires two complete sampling rounds spaced at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient. The current confirmatory set comprises forty-eight samples with zero E. coli positives across all locations [CIPHER].\",\"old\":\"Clearance requires two complete sampling rounds spaced at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient [CIPHER].\"},{\"new\":\"Emergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock; the duration is not thirty-six days and excludes mobile-pump load [ECHO]. The grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW; rated power is not usable power [ECHO]. KESTREL diesel stock covers emergency load for 36 hours and full pump load for 22 hours; these load regimes are distinct and must not be merged as a single duration [KESTREL, ECHO]. Coagulant and chlorine chemical stocks provide 4.5 days and 3.2 days of treatment capacity respectively; inventory duration is not delivery lead time [KESTREL, FALCON]. Staffing continuity depends on mutual-aid logistics; current shift coverage must be verified against the 36-hour generator window [KESTREL]. Any change to ECHO power state or KESTREL fuel stock makes prior pump sequencing evidence stale [DELTA, ECHO, KESTREL]. The shared transmission main is capped at 14.5 million gallons per day, and pump nameplate capacities cannot be summed into usable system flow; the latest inspected configuration sustained 12.8 MGD after fire-flow and hospital reserve [DELTA]. Restoration may advance through ten, thirty, sixty, and one hundred percent demand stages only after two consecutive thirty-minute windows meet pressure, turbidity, power, and storage gates [DELTA]. The shared-main limit under staged demand requires that DELTA pump capacity not exceed the 6.5 MW usable grid feed plus any available generator margin without triggering cavitation constraints [DELTA, ECHO, BASTION].\",\"old\":\"Emergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock; the duration is not thirty-six days and excludes mobile-pump load [ECHO]. The grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW; rated power is not usable power [ECHO]. KESTREL diesel stock covers emergency load for 36 hours and full pump load for 22 hours; these load regimes are distinct and must not be merged as a single duration [KESTREL, ECHO]. Coagulant and chlorine chemical stocks provide 4.5 days and 3.2 days of treatment capacity respectively; inventory duration is not delivery lead time [KESTREL, FALCON]. Staffing continuity depends on mutual-aid logistics; current shift coverage must be verified against the 36-hour generator window [KESTREL]. Any change to ECHO power state or KESTREL fuel stock makes prior pump sequencing evidence stale [DELTA, ECHO, KESTREL]. The shared-main limit under staged demand requires that DELTA pump capacity not exceed the 6.5 MW usable grid feed plus any available generator margin without triggering cavitation constraints [DELTA, ECHO, BASTION].\"},{\"new\":\"Critical-signal telemetry coverage stands at 96 percent, with 4 percent of monitored points unobserved; this coverage gap does not prove the uninstrumented zones are healthy, only that they are not currently observable [INDIGO]. Telemetry delay is 700 milliseconds at p95 and 1,200 milliseconds at p99; both are observations, not control deadlines [INDIGO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states; a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Telemetry delays in the unobserved 4 percent create uncertainty that must be treated as potential adverse condition until verified by direct observation or alternate telemetry [INDIGO]. Warnings versus actions: a pressure warning at 38 psi requires monitoring and logging but does not require isolation; an isolation trigger at 30 psi requires immediate valve closure and zone separation [INDIGO, BASTION]. Any change to hydraulic model H12, pump plan P9, or control-system key set W4 invalidates prior telemetry correlation evidence and requires re-verification of coverage and alert thresholds [MOSAIC, INDIGO, BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON]. Alternate telemetry paths must be identified for the 4 percent unobserved zone before closure can be claimed [INDIGO, NEXUS].\",\"old\":\"Critical-signal telemetry coverage stands at 96 percent, with 4 percent of monitored points unobserved; this coverage gap does not prove the uninstrumented zones are healthy, only that they are not currently observable [INDIGO]. Pressure warnings at 38 psi and isolation triggers at 30 psi are distinct control states; a warning does not initiate isolation, and an isolation trigger does not merely warn [INDIGO, BASTION]. Telemetry delays in the unobserved 4 percent create uncertainty that must be treated as potential adverse condition until verified by direct observation or alternate telemetry [INDIGO]. Warnings versus actions: a pressure warning at 38 psi requires monitoring and logging but does not require isolation; an isolation trigger at 30 psi requires immediate valve closure and zone separation [INDIGO, BASTION]. Any change to hydraulic model H12, pump plan P9, or control-system key set W4 invalidates prior telemetry correlation evidence and requires re-verification of coverage and alert thresholds [MOSAIC, INDIGO, BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON]. Alternate telemetry paths must be identified for the 4 percent unobserved zone before closure can be claimed [INDIGO, NEXUS].\"}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v009:56dbd283bef7636af26b7cad3d0fcbf11b3b6421664fb77dee67cced063e254d\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-019\",\"result_kind\